course: dictionary
lesson: 3231
title: Entitle: the right to have it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To entitle someone to something means to give them the right to have or do it. «Rights are things every person is entitled to, such as safety, education, being heard and freedom of belief.» So being entitled to education means you have a right to go to school, and nobody can take that away from you.
explain: Entitle has another meaning: to give a book, film or poem its title. «A poem entitled "The Sea" was read to the class.» Here entitled means the poem was given the name "The Sea". Ask yourself: is someone getting a right, or is something getting a name? The words around it tell you which.
explain: Entitled can also be an adjective, and it describes behaviour. Someone with an entitled attitude thinks they deserve special treatment, even when they have not earned it. This is not a kind word, so check the sentence before you use it.
fact: Entitle is a verb: entitle, entitles, entitled, entitling.
fact: «Entitle» means to give someone the right to have or do something.
fact: «Entitled to» is followed by the thing you have a right to, as in «entitled to a refund».
fact: «Entitle» can also mean to give a book, film or poem a title.
fact: «Entitled» as an adjective means thinking you deserve special treatment.
exercise: «Every child is entitled to education.» What does entitled mean here? | Is bored by | Is tired of | Is afraid of | *Has the right to
exercise: «The poet entitled her book "Night Birds".» What does entitled mean here? | *Gave it the name Night Birds | Lost it at school | Gave it away for free | Put it on a shelf
exercise: Ellie says Jack has an entitled attitude. What does that suggest? | Jack is hungry | Jack is very kind and shares | Jack is new at school | *Jack thinks he deserves special treatment
test: «If the shoes break in a week, you are entitled to a refund.» What does entitled to a refund mean? | You are sad about the shop | *You have the right to get your money back | You must pay extra | You have to keep the shoes
test: «The film was entitled "The Lost Map".» What does entitled mean here? | It was made in a hurry | It was too long to watch | It was given to the cinema | *It was given the title The Lost Map
exam: Which sentence uses entitle to mean having a right? | The cake was entitled Chocolate Dream | He entitled the poem in a hurry | The dog entitled the cat to its bed | *Everyone who buys a ticket is entitled to a seat
